  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRRS Yemen 2024 &#x2013; WHO IPC/WASH Specialist</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assignment at the request of the WHO Infection Prevention and Control (IPC)/Water, Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH).In the northern governorates of Yemen, an Acute Watery Diarrhea (AWD) has been declared with, and rapid increase in cases over the last 2 weeks (more than 2,000 suspected cases in week 11 and 12, 2024 with 28 associated death). There is also an increase in confirmed cholera cases in the Southern governorates and response will be scaled up.WHO WASH response needs to scale up quickly, to given the rapid increase of cases and weak WASH capacities in the country. An experienced international WASH officer is urgently required to support development detailed and prioritized WASH response plan for the North and supervise the implementation of WHO WASH response. The outbreak response is significantly underfunded and no funds for surge support consultants are available.</narrative>
  </description>
